  * panel stays lit and this black overlay shows the time, the date, the battery and one icon per app
  * with notifications. Black pixels cost nothing on OLED; the text is dim grey. The content moves a
  * little every minute so no pixel stays lit for long.
+ *
+ * With a panel that keeps a clock of its own (the S10e's S6E3FA7: a `self_clock` attribute next to `lpm`), the
+ * AOD is Samsung's: once it shows, the panel goes into its low power mode and draws analog hands over a dial
+ * drawn here, ticking by itself while the phone sleeps; the panel moves the picture against burn-in. Nothing
+ * needs to wake the phone for the time then (s10e-sleepd sees the clock run). Waking, the panel leaves low
+ * power mode before the AOD fades out. If the panel refuses, the AOD shows the time as before.
  */
 
 #define AOD_SHIFT 24 /* px the content wanders, against burn-in */
+#define AOD_LPM_NITS "10"
+/* the dial around the panel's hands, in panel pixels: they reach 207 px from the centre (s6e3fa7 hand image) */
+#define DIAL_TICK_OUT 236.0
+#define DIAL_TICK_IN  218.0
+#define DIAL_QUARTER_IN 204.0
+#define DIAL_DOT 9.0
 
